;; Classic call/cc-based generator/coroutine (SICP-style): a producer
;; captures a continuation each time it "yields", handing control back to
;; the consumer; the consumer re-enters the producer's saved continuation
;; repeatedly, resuming deep inside a producer call that returned long ago.
;; This is the shape real generator/amb libraries need re-entrant
;; continuations for.
;;
;; MEASURED BEHAVIOR (2026-08-25, .icc/silent-wrong-ledger.yaml SW-51/SW-52):
;;   native JIT (-r): CRASHES on the SECOND yield — SIGSEGV, after correctly
;;                    printing "gen1: 1". Same escape-only cause as
;;                    reentry_after_function_return.esk (SW-51).
;;   native AOT:      Same SIGSEGV, same point.
;;   bytecode VM:     Does NOT crash, but is SILENTLY WRONG (SW-52, exit 0,
;;                    no diagnostic): instead of the correct
;;                      gen1: 1 / gen2: 2 / gen3: 3 / gen4: done
;;                    it prints a garbled interleaving that replays the
;;                    producer's internal 1/2/3/done sequence under the
;;                    wrong "genN:" labels (observed: gen1:1, gen2:2,
;;                    gen2:3, gen2:done, gen2:1, gen3:2, gen3:3, gen3:done,
;;                    gen3:1, gen4:2, gen4:3, gen4:done, gen4:1, done) —
;;                    every re-invocation replays more of the top-level
;;                    program than it should, rather than resuming exactly
;;                    at the yield point as seen by the consumer.
;;
;; This fixture is deliberately NOT wired into any pass/fail CI harness
;; (native crashes by design here, and the VM's wrong output has no
;; syntactic PASS/FAIL marker to key a gate on — the point is the exact
;; transcript). Run manually, e.g.:
;;   ESHKOL_VM_NO_DISASM=1 ./build/eshkol-vm-standalone-test \
;;     tests/continuations/generator_coroutine.esk
(define return-k #f)
(define resume-k #f)

(define (yield v)
  (call/cc (lambda (k)
    (set! resume-k k)
    (return-k v))))

(define (producer)
  (call/cc (lambda (ret)
    (set! return-k ret)
    (yield 1)
    (yield 2)
    (yield 3)
    (return-k 'done))))

(define (next!)
  (if resume-k
      (let ((k resume-k))
        (set! resume-k #f)
        (k 'go))
      (producer)))

(display "gen1: ") (display (next!)) (newline)
(display "gen2: ") (display (next!)) (newline)
(display "gen3: ") (display (next!)) (newline)
(display "gen4: ") (display (next!)) (newline)
(display "done") (newline)
